      "code_path": "contracts/protocol/sources/internal/market/market.move::ensure_liquidate_borrow_allowed::L927-1013",
      "proof_trace": "The proof fails: the code enforces `repay_amount <= debt_balance * close_factor` (L1008-1011) — a static global parameter — instead of the dynamic formula R_max = (WD - WC) / (w_d - LT_liq × (1+incentive)) required to bring weighted_debts' == weighted_collateral' (risk == 1.0). For a barely-unhealthy position (e.g., WD=1021, WC=1020, LTV_liq=0.85, incentive=0.05), R_max ≈ 9.3 but close_factor×D ≈ 510, allowing ~55× over-liquidation; the spec INV-001 and the module comment in liquidate.move explicitly require the cap to equal R_max.",
      "attack_scenario": "A whitelisted LiquidationBot calls `liquidate()` on an obligation that is barely unhealthy (weighted_debts just above weighted_collateral by ε). The bot supplies `available_repay_coin = close_factor × debt_balance`, which passes the close_factor assertion but is orders of magnitude larger than R_max for that position; the borrower loses up to 50% of their total debt in collateral (at the liquidation incentive premium) when less than 1% repayment was sufficient to restore health.",
      "checklist_id": "PROP-current-fina-inv-014"
    }
  ]
}

